# Website change audit

After a change that alters what visitors or staff see, or how the site behaves, draft the Hebrew rows in the same reply and wait for confirmation before recording them. Do not end that reply without the drafts. The task is not finished while a visible change is still unlogged and unconfirmed.

One row per distinct change. Unrelated changes, and changes that sit in different sections, are separate rows even when they are made together. Do not merge them into one summary. Edits that belong to the same section and describe one change can share a row.

If more site edits land before confirmation, update the matching draft or add another row, then show every pending row again. Do not fold a different section into an existing draft.

Each row has:

- `date`: `YYYY-MM-DD` in Asia/Jerusalem
- `summary`: Hebrew, what changed
- `area`: Hebrew page name
- `section`: Hebrew heading on that page, when the change sits in a section
- `href`: site path, with a hash when there is a section, for example `/Useful_links/Social_Work_Resources#wishes`

Show the draft and stop. Prepend it to `src/data/change-log.json` only after an explicit yes or an edited wording. Do not commit the row before that reply. Newest row stays first.

```json
{
  "date": "2026-10-06",
  "summary": "במשאלות ופרידה נוספו פרטים על אמבולנס המשאלות.",
  "area": "תמיכה בעובדים סוציאליים",
  "section": "משאלות ופרידה",
  "href": "/Useful_links/Social_Work_Resources#wishes"
}
```

Skip the audit when asked not to log it, and for work that does not change the site (questions, investigation, formatting-only cleanup).
